WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.200
SmartVest Investing Academy.

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.862
Lesson 8: What is SIP?

3
00:00:05.862 --> 00:00:15.363
How can a salaried professional or student build a multi-lakh portfolio without saving up a massive lump sum or stressing over market timing?

4
00:00:15.363 --> 00:00:23.738
In India, the most popular and disciplined way to invest is through a SIP—which stands for Systematic Investment Plan.

5
00:00:23.738 --> 00:00:32.950
A SIP is NOT a separate investment product or asset class; it is an automated METHOD of investing regularly into mutual funds.

6
00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:52.438
Instead of waiting to accumulate ₹1 Lakh and trying to guess the 'perfect day' to invest, a SIP automatically debits a fixed chosen amount—such as ₹1,000, ₹5,000, or ₹10,000—from your bank account at scheduled intervals, usually once a month.

7
00:00:52.438 --> 00:00:57.525
The core mathematical superpower of a SIP is Rupee Cost Averaging.

8
00:00:57.525 --> 00:01:01.625
Let us see how it works across market cycles:

9
00:01:01.625 --> 00:01:15.487
When the stock market drops and fund NAV falls from ₹100 to ₹80, your fixed ₹5,000 monthly SIP automatically buys MORE units—62.5 units instead of 50.

10
00:01:15.487 --> 00:01:24.362
When the market rises and NAV climbs to ₹125, your ₹5,000 buys FEWER units—40 units.

11
00:01:24.362 --> 00:01:32.812
Over time, this automatically lowers your average purchase price per unit without you ever having to watch market charts.

12
00:01:32.812 --> 00:01:38.938
You naturally buy more when assets are discounted and buy less when they are expensive.

13
00:01:38.938 --> 00:01:45.287
A common mistake is believing that an SIP guarantees positive returns or removes all risk.

14
00:01:45.287 --> 00:01:53.188
An SIP manages timing risk and builds habit, but the underlying fund value will still fluctuate with market trends.

15
00:01:53.188 --> 00:01:58.550
The biggest mistake investors make is stopping their SIPs when markets fall.

16
00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:05.500
Stopping during downturns destroys the rupee cost averaging advantage right when units are cheapest.

17
00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:14.963
An SIP turns regular monthly savings into automated investing, leveraging rupee cost averaging to build long-term wealth with discipline.

18
00:02:14.963 --> 00:02:18.013
